            <ArticleTitle>Postoperative analgesia for day-case herniorrhaphy patients. A comparison of cryoanalgesia, paravertebral blockade and oral analgesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>603-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients were admitted as day-cases for inguinal herniorrhaphy under epidural anaesthesia and chlormethiazole sedation. The patients were given oral analgesia, and in addition, some were given either a paravertebral block with a dextran/bupivacaine mixture or cryoanalgesia of the ilio-inguinal nerve for postoperative pain relief. These anaesthetic and analgesic techniques are discussed in relation to day-case herniorrhaphy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
